  "advisoryPlan": "### Advisory Plan: Instrument State Machine\n\n**1. Named Nodes (States)**\n*   **Idle**: Rounded rectangle, fill `#e5efeb`, stroke `#355c53`.\n*   **Running**: Rounded rectangle, fill `#e5efeb`, stroke `#355c53`.\n*   **Paused**: Rounded rectangle, fill `#e5efeb`, stroke `#355c53`.\n*   **Completed**: Rounded rectangle, fill `#e5efeb`, stroke `#355c53`.\n    *   *Note:* All states appear exactly once. \"Completed\" is treated as a standard state node (not terminal) to accommodate the return transition.\n\n**2. Initial Marker**\n*   **Anonymous Dot**: Solid circle, fill/stroke `#355c53`.\n*   **Relationship**: Directed edge from Anonymous Dot → **Idle**.\n*   *Constraint Check:* Renderer supports \"explicitly unnamed initial: dot\". No label required on this specific entry arrow per methodology.\n\n**3. Transitions (Edges & Events)**\nAll edges are orthogonal polylines with filled triangle arrows (`#355c53`). Labels are English event names, positioned to avoid overlap.\n\n| Source | Target | Event Label | Layout Note |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Idle | Running | start | Primary forward flow |\n| Running | Paused | pause | Branch from Running |\n| Paused | Running | resume | Return loop (likely below or above main flow) |\n| Running | Completed | finish | Forward flow continuation |\n| Paused | Idle | cancel | Long-range return loop (requires routing around nodes) |\n| Completed | Idle | reset | Cycle closure (requires routing around nodes) |\n\n**4. Visual Style & Constraints**\n*   **Palette:** Background white; Node fill `#e5efeb`; Stroke/Arrow `#355c53`; Text `#203d37`.\n*   **Typography:** Noto Sans regular, normal style. Min 14px at 1K resolution.\n*   **Geometry:** Flat vector only. No shadows, filters, or curves.\n*   **Layout Direction:** RIGHT is the primary hint for the main sequence (Idle→Running→...), but ELK will compute exact coordinates to handle the feedback loops (resume, cancel, reset) without overlap.\n\n**5. Compliance & Evidence Gaps**\n*   **Met Requirements:** All 4 states present; Initial dot enters Idle; All 6 transitions labeled with events; Completed connects back to Idle; English text used.\n*   **Reference Usage:** Structural design (state transition topology) derived from methodology. Visual style (colors/shapes) aligned with renderer contract and reference tone, but no scientific data copied.\n*   **Uncertainties:** None. The topology is fully defined and supported by the `elkjs` topology renderer capabilities (orthogonal routing handles cycles).\n\n**6. Review Checklist**\n*   [ ] Verify \"Completed\" node has an outgoing arrow labeled \"reset\".\n*   [ ] Verify \"Idle\" node has incoming arrows from \"Anonymous Dot\", \"Paused\" (cancel), and \"Completed\" (reset).\n*   [ ] Ensure \"cancel\" and \"reset\" arrows do not visually cross through state nodes.\n*   [ ] Confirm font size $\\ge$ 14px.",
